1. Unit test
Unit test is test for individual method or component. It's a white box test, usually done by developer.
Common tools are Junit, Mockito.

2. Functional test
Test specific features or business logics

3. Integration test
Test for multiple components. The scope can be small to an api to large from front-end to back-end.
Common tool is TestNG.

4. Regression test
Make sure new changes don't break tests.

5. Smoke test
Test core functions.

6. Performance test
Load test, how app works in high traffic.

7. Stress test
How system behave under extreme load. It goal is to see the extreme point and how system recover.

8. AB test
We have a control group and a variant group, show different features to people, to test whether the new feature
is better

9. End to end test
Test the entire workflow, from front-end to back-end to database, also include any external systems, simulate
how user use the app.

10. User acceptance test
Final stage of test, real users test the app too see if it meets business requirements.